Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Offset: in the arc join, a wall whose edges to a rounding vanishing beside a
removed face are a chain is extended to the removed face as one section
(mitcad#2535).

GitHub #645's loft with its top rounded 2 mm, shelled 3 mm with the top
open and Rounded corners (the arc join): the rounding along the slot's near
round end and the crease's sliver vanish (patch 2494), and the wall across
them has 21 edges to them, the top 35. ToContext (patch 2463) extended the
wall to the top along the one wall edge each top edge was paired with
first (four of the 21 were left out), ExtentFace gave each extended edge
the whole section of the wall with the top, and the vertices between them
had no place on it: the third top edge got a section of no length as its
image, and ContextIntByArc's OrientSection raised Standard_ConstructionError.

ToContext now extends the kept face along every edge paired across with
the removed face's edge (KeptFacesAcrossToCap). ExtentFace takes a run of
two or more consecutive edges of a wire that are across vanishing faces and
are extended to the same face as one edge from the run's first vertex to
its last (RunsToOneStop): one section, bounded where the edges beside the
run meet it, the image of every edge of the run. ToContext binds that
section to the face and as the image of one of the removed face's edges
across once, and ContextIntByArc stores it on the removed face once.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2535.

